# CODEOWNERS for puller
#
# Why this exists (public-repo review control):
# On a public repo, anyone can open a PR, but CODEOWNERS lets you require
# review from the named user before any path can be merged into main. If
# you (or a future collaborator) forget to enforce review-required on main,
# CODEOWNERS is the last line of defense: the repo-level "Require review
# from Code Owners" toggle will hold any PR that touches owned paths.
#
# Scope: entire repo owned by @ryanrestivo. If you add collaborators, add
# their handles here on top of (or in lieu of) the single-owner line.
#
# Note: for CODEOWNERS to have any effect, you must ALSO enable in
# Settings → Branches → main:
#   - "Require pull request reviews before merging"
#   - "Require review from Code Owners"
# I did not change that setting (I don't have write access to repo settings
# from here). See PR body item (h).

*   @ryanrestivo

# Sensitive paths worth double-checking before merge (defense-in-depth even
# with a single owner; becomes meaningful if you add a second collaborator):
.github/workflows/   @ryanrestivo
requirements.txt      @ryanrestivo
